/**
 * @module json
 *
 * Encodes and decodes JSON.
 *
 * JSON (JavaScript Object Notation) is a lightweight, text-based data
 * interchange format that doesn't depend on any language. It was
 * derived from the ECMAScript standard, and defines a small set of
 * formatting rules for representing structured data in a portable way.
 *
 * This implementation follows [RFC
 * 8259](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8259).
 *
 * ### How JSON values are decoded
 *
 * | JSON | Zuri |
 * |------|-------|
 * | null | `nil` |
 * | string | string |
 * | number | number |
 * | boolean | bool |
 * | array | list |
 * | object | dict |
 *
 * ### How Zuri values are encoded
 *
 * | Zuri | JSON |
 * |-------|------|
 * | `nil` | null |
 * | number | number |
 * | string | string |
 * | list | array |
 * | dict | object |
 * | An instance of a class with a `@to_json` method | whatever that method returns |
 *
 * For example:
 *
 * ```zuri-repl
 * %> import json
 * %> json.encode([1, 2, 3])
 * '[1,2,3]'
 * %>
 * %> json.encode({name: 'Zuri', version: '0.1.0'})
 * '{"name":"Zuri","version":"0.1.0"}'
 * %>
 * %> json.encode({name: 'Zuri', version: '0.1.0'}, false)
 * '{
 *   "name": "Zuri",
 *   "version": "0.1.0"
 * }'
 * ```
 *
 * @copyright 2021, Richard Ore and Zuri contributors
 */

/**
 * JSON encodes the given value with a recursive depth up to
 * `max_depth`.
 *
 * If _compact_ is `true`, the resulting json string will be
 * tightly packed. i.e. spaces will be trimmed from objects and
 * arrays. Otherwise, the JSON output will be pretty formatted.
 *
 * @param any value
 * @param ?bool compact: Default value is `true`.
 * @param ?number max_depth: is the maximum recursive depth for
 *    encoding, default = 1024.
 * @note pretty formatting use 2 spaces instead of tabs.
 * @raises Error: If the value cannot be encoded to json.
 * @returns string
 */
def encode(value, compact, max_depth) {}

/**
 * Decodes the input JSON string into Zuri objects
 *
 * @param string value: The string to decode
 * @param ?bool allow_comments: Can be set to enable/disable
 *    C-style comments in json [default = true]
 * @raises Error: If the json is invalid.
 * @returns object
 */
def decode(value, allow_comments) {}

/**
 * Parses a file containing json data.
 *
 * @param string path
 * @param ?bool allow_comments: Can be set to enable/disable
 *    C-style comments in json [default = true]
 * @raises Error: If the file cannot be read or if the json is
 *    invalid.
 * @returns object
 */
def parse(path, allow_comments) {}

/**
 * Dumps the given value into a json file at the specified path.
 *
 * @param any value
 * @param string path
 * @param ?bool compact: Default value is `true`.
 * @param ?number max_depth: is the maximum recursive depth for
 *    encoding, default = 1024.
 * @note pretty formatting use 2 spaces instead of tabs.
 * @raises Error: If the file cannot be written to.
 */
def dump(value, path, compact, max_depth) {}
